   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "MONTOYA LTD MEDICAL - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\n\nPatient: Maria Richardson\nDOB: 09/13/1993\nSex: F\nMRN: 392800\n\nAdmit Date: 08/21/2013\nDischarge Date: 08/23/2013\nAttending Physician: Dr. Marie Duncan, Family Medicine\n\n**Principal Diagnosis:**\nHypertension (controlled with 1 agent; bp band >180/110)\n\n**Secondary Diagnoses:**\n- Glaucoma\n- Musculoskeletal injury\n- Acne\n\n**Hospital Course:**\n\nMs. Maria Richardson, a 29-year-old female, was admitted on 08/21/2013 with a principal diagnosis of hypertension. She has a history of controlled hypertension managed with hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg. On admission, her blood pressure was recorded at 180/106 mmHg, and her weight was 155 lbs. \n\nDuring her hospital stay, Ms. Richardson's hypertension was closely monitored. She continued her home medication regimen, which included hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg daily. No acute changes or complications were noted during her stay. Her blood pressure readings fluctuated but remained within a controlled range with the current medication.\n\nMs. Richardson also has a history of glaucoma, managed with latanoprost 0.005% eye drops. She reported no changes or symptoms related to her glaucoma during this admission. \n\nAdditionally, she has a history of a musculoskeletal injury, for which she takes cyclobenzaprine 10 mg and ibuprofen 800 mg as needed. She denied any acute musculoskeletal complaints during this admission. \n\nLastly, Ms. Richardson has acne, managed with tretinoin 0.05% topical cream. She reported no new or worsening acne lesions during her hospital stay.\n\n**Procedures:**\nNo procedures were performed during this admission.\n\n**Discharge Medications:**\n- Hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg daily for hypertension\n- Latanoprost 0.005% eye drops nightly for glaucoma\n- Cyclobenzaprine 10 mg as needed for musculoskeletal pain\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg as needed for pain\n- Tretinoin 0.05% topical cream nightly for acne\n\n**Follow-Up:**\nMs. Richardson was discharged home in stable condition on 08/23/2013. She was advised to continue her current medication regimen and follow up with her primary care physician, Dr. Marie Duncan, within one week for a post-discharge evaluation. She was also instructed to monitor her blood pressure at home and report any readings consistently above 180/110 mmHg.\n\n**Social History:**\n- Tobacco use: Former cigarette smoker, 10 cigarettes per day, quit on 01/26/2023.\n- Alcohol use: Approximately 2 drinks per week.\n- Family history: Father has COPD, onset at age 72, currently 91 years old and living.\n\n**Review of Systems:**\n- Constitutional: Denied fever, chills, or weight los"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "s.\n- Eyes: No changes in vision or eye pain.\n- Cardiovascular: No chest pain or palpitations.\n- Respiratory: No shortness of breath or cough.\n- Gastrointestinal: No nausea, vomiting, or changes in bowel habits.\n- Musculoskeletal: No joint pain or swelling.\n- Skin: No new rashes or lesions.\n\n**Physical Examination on Discharge:**\n- Vital signs: Blood pressure 178/104 mmHg, heart rate 76 bpm, respiratory rate 18 breaths per minute, temperature 98.6°F.\n- General: Well-nourished, well-developed female in no acute distress.\n- HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. Eyes: Pupils equal, round, reactive to light. No conjunctival injection. \n- Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops.\n- Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, no hepatosplenomegaly.\n- Musculoskeletal: No deformities, full range of motion in all joints.\n- Skin: Clear, no lesions or rashes.\n\n**Discharge Instructions:**\nMs. Richardson was provided with detailed instructions regarding her medication regimen, the importance of regular follow-up appointments, and monitoring her blood pressure at home. She was advised to maintain a healthy lifestyle, including a balanced diet and regular physical activity, to help manage her hypertension.\n\n**Signature:**\nDr. Marie Duncan\nFamily Medicine\nMontoya Ltd Medical Group\n"
